oads, meta. Used by every `server/document.js`. |\n| `Body` | component | `src/server/renderer/document/Body.jsx:13` | Public. Renders `&lt;body&gt;` with hydration state script tags. |\n\n**1.1a — The `react-router-dom` wildcard is the biggest freeze hazard.** `src/index.jsx:1` re-exports all 76 names, including the 11 explicitly-unstable ones:\n\n```\nUNSAFE_DataRouterContext, UNSAFE_DataRouterStateContext, UNSAFE_ErrorResponseImpl,\nUNSAFE_FetchersContext, UNSAFE_LocationContext, UNSAFE_NavigationContext,\nUNSAFE_RouteContext, UNSAFE_ViewTransitionContext, UNSAFE_useRouteId,\nUNSAFE_useScrollRestoration, unstable_HistoryRouter, unstable_usePrompt\n```\n\nFreezing `.` as-is means freezing react-router v6's `UNSAFE_*`/`unstable_*` API as Catalyst public API, and pins you to `react-router-dom@^6.16.0` (`package.json:53`) — a v7 bump becomes a breaking change for Catalyst. Consumers actually use only 6 router names: `Link`, `Outlet`, `RouterProvider`, `useParams`, `useNavigate`, `createBrowserRouter` (the last only inside `ClientRouter.js:1`).\n\n---\n\n### 1.2 `./logger` → `src/logger.js`\n\n| Export | Kind | Line | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `configureLogger` | fn | `src/logger.js:81` | Winston logger with daily-rotate file transports (info/debug/error). Returns `Logger`, **and assigns `global.logger`** (`:77`) as a side effect. |\n\nNotes: no default export. The `global.logger` mutation at `:77` is an undeclared part of the contract — `src/otel.js` (`:87`, `:96`, `:110`, `:125`…) calls bare `logger.*` and will `ReferenceError` if `configureLogger` was never called. `Logger.debug` is a silent no-op stub when `enableDebugLogs` is falsy (`:59`).\n\n---\n\n### 1.3 `./caching` → `src/caching.js`\n\n```js\nexport * from \"@tata1mg/api-caching\"\n```\n\n**This entry point is broken.** `@tata1mg/api-caching` is:\n- **not** in `dependencies` or `peerDependencies` (`packages/catalyst-core/package.json:44-72`)\n- **not** installed anywhere in the monorepo (`node_modules/@tata1mg/` does not exist)\n- never imported by any consumer in `examples/`, `apps/`, `docs/content/`, or the CCA templates\n\nAny `import ... from \"catalyst-core/caching\"` throws `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND` today. Its export surface is unknowable from this repo. **Strong candidate for removal from the exports map before a freeze** — you cannot freeze an API you cannot enumerate.\n\n---\n\n### 1.4 `./router/ClientRouter` → `src/router/ClientRouter.js`\n\n| Export | Kind | Line | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `default` (`clientRouter`) | fn | `src/router/ClientRouter.js:15` | `({routerInitialState}) =&gt; createBrowserRouter(preparedRoutes(...))`. |\n\n**Two side effects on import**, both undocumented:\n- `src/router/ClientRouter.js:5` — calls `registerCatalystServiceWorker()` at module scope. Merely importing registers a service worker.\n- `src/router/ClientRouter.js:2` — `import { preparedRoutes } from \"@catalyst/template/src/js/routes/utils\"`. This module **cannot resolve** unless the consumer's build applies the alias (see §6). It is not resolvable by plain Node/bundlers.\n\nDefault-only export with no named export; `clientRouter` is not accessible by name.\n\n---\n\n### 1.5 `./document` → `src/server/renderer/document/index.jsx`\n\n| Export | Kind | Line |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Head` | component | `src/server/renderer/document/Head.jsx:10` |\n| `Body` | component | `src/server/renderer/document/Body.jsx:13` |\n\n**Fully redundant.** `src/index.jsx:8` already does `export * from \"./server/renderer/document/index.jsx\"`, so `Head`/`Body` are reachable from `\".\"`. Every consumer in the repo imports them from `\"catalyst-core\"`, **not** `\"catalyst-core/document\"` — I found zero uses of the `./document` specifier anywhere (`docs/`, `examples/`, `apps/`, `packages/create-catalyst-app/templates/common/server/document.js:2` all use the root). Candidate for removal, or make it the canonical path and drop the root re-export.\n\n---\n\n### 1.6 `./WebBridge` → `src/native/bridge/WebBridge.js`\n\n| Export | Kind | Line | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `default` (`WebBridge` **instance**) | object | `src/native/bridge/WebBridge.js:533` | Singleton instance of `class WebBridge` (`:66`). |\n\nThe class is not exported; only the instance is. Public instance surface (all class fields, so all enumerable own properties — none can be tree-shaken or marked private):\n\n| Member | Line | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `WebBridge.init` | `:88` | **static.** Idempotent-ish; assigns `window.WebBridge`, conditionally lazy-loads the perf collector when `window.__CATALYST_PROFILER_ENABLED === true` (`:105`). Documented entry point. |\n| `callback(interfaceName, data)` | `:120` | Native→JS dispatch. Internal protocol surface. |\n| `register(interfaceName, callback)` | `:158` | Register a native callback handler. |\n| `unregister(interfaceName)` | `:187` | |\n| `isRegistered(interfaceName)` | `:203` | |\n| `getRegisteredInterfaces()` | `:211` | |\n| `getHandler(interfaceName)` | `:220` | Leaks internal handler refs. |\n| `clearAll()` | `:227` | |\n| `debug()` | `:236` | **Dev-tooling leak.** |\n| `testCallback(name, testData)` | `:258` | **Dev-only** — early-returns unless `NODE_ENV === \"development\"` (`:259`). Should not be public. |\n| `_logInitialization()` | `:76` | **Underscore-prefixed private, but publicly reachable.** Clear internal leak. |\n| `requestHapticFeedback(type)` | `:273` | Duplicates the `./hooks` export of the same name (`hooks/useHapticFeedback.js:8`) with a **different default**: `\"VIRTUAL_KEY\"` here vs `\"light\"` there. |\n| `openCamera(options)` | `:307` | Duplicates `useCamera` machinery. |\n| `requestCameraPermission(config)` | `:316` | Duplicates the `./hooks` export (`hooks/useCamera.js:191`). |\n| `getDeviceInfoFromLegacyBridge(parseDeviceInfo)` | `:320` | **Legacy path, publicly reachable.** |\n| `getDeviceInfoFromPluginBridge(parseDeviceInfo)` | `:361` | Internal transport detail. |\n| `shouldFallbackToLegacyDeviceInfo(error)` | `:454` | **Internal heuristic, publicly reachable.** |\n| `getDeviceInfo(...)` | ~`:520` | The documented one (`docs/content/11-API Reference/01-Hooks.md:200`). |\n\nOnly `init()` and `getDeviceInfo()` are documented. Everything else is de-facto public by virtue of being an instance field. Freezing this as-is locks in `_logInitialization`, `testCallback`, `debug`, and both legacy device-info paths.\n\n---\n\n### 1.7 `./hooks` → `src/native/bridge/hooks.js` → `src/native/bridge/hooks/index.js`\n\n18 exports. `hooks.js:1` is a one-line `export * from \"./hooks/index.js\"` indirection.\n\n**React hooks (13):**\n\n| Export | Line | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `useAI` | `hooks/useAI.js:46` | Cloud/local/native AI. **Soft-depends on the un-declared `catalyst-ai` package** via `require(\"catalyst-ai\")` in a try/catch (`useAI.js:35`) and the build-injected `__CATALYST_PACKAGES__` global. `catalyst-ai` is a workspace package (`packages/catalyst-ai`, v0.1.0) but is **not** a dependency/peerDependency/optionalDependency of catalyst-core. |\n| `useGoogleSignIn` | `hooks/useGoogleSignIn.js:8` | Native Google sign-in. Note: takes `defaultOptions` — the only hook not using the `{webFallback}` convention. |\n| `useCamera` | `hooks/useCamera.js:7` | Native camera capture. |\n| `useCameraPermission` | `hooks/useCamera.js:225` | Camera permission state. |\n| `useIntent` | `hooks/useIntent.js:7` | Android intents. Takes **no** options arg — inconsistent with siblings. |\n| `useFilePicker` | `hooks/useFilePicker.js:165` | Native file picker. |\n| `useHapticFeedback` | `hooks/useHapticFeedback.js:64` | Haptics. |\n| `useNotification` | `hooks/useNotification.js:114` | Push notifications. Takes no args. |\n| `useNotificationPermission` | `hooks/useNotification.js:69` | Takes no args. |\n| `useNetworkStatus` | `hooks/useNetworkStatus.js:7` | Online/offline + connection type. |\n| `useDeviceInfo` | `hooks/useDeviceInfo.js:5` | Device/screen/app metadata. |\n| `useDataProtection` | `hooks/useDataProtection.js:8` | Screenshot/recording protection. |\n| `useSafeArea` | `hooks/useSafeArea.js:6` | Safe-area insets. |\n| `useVideoStream` | `hooks/useVideoStream.js:16` | Camera video stream + QR detection. Signature `{onQRDetected, webFallback}` is unlike all others. |\n| `useNativeTransition` | `hooks/useNativeTransition.js:29` | Native screen transitions. Takes `defaults` not `{webFallback}`. |\n\n**Non-hooks exported from an entry point named `./hooks` (4)** — naming/placement inconsistency:\n\n| Export | Line | Issue |\n|---|---|---|\n| `requestCameraPermission` | `hooks/useCamera.js:191` | Imperative fn, not a hook. Also duplicated on `WebBridge:316`. |\n| `requestHapticFeedback` | `hooks/useHapticFeedback.js:8` | Imperative fn. Duplicated on `WebBridge:273` **with a different default arg** (`\"light\"` vs `\"VIRTUAL_KEY\"`). |\n| `requestNotificationPermission` | `hooks/useNotification.js:36` | Imperative fn. |\n| `sanitizeFilePickerOptions` | `hooks/useFilePicker.js:44` | **Internal-only leak.** A validation helper for the hook's own args; no consumer or doc uses it. Should not be public. |\n\n---\n\n### 1.8 `./sentry` → `src/sentry.cjs` (built from `src/sentry.js`)\n\n| Export | Kind | Line | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `init` | fn | `src/sentry.js:31` | Reads `process.env.SENTRY_CONFIG` JSON, calls `Sentry.init`. Idempotency guarded by module-level `sentryInitialized` (`:3`). |\n| `captureException` | fn | `src/sentry.js:79` | |\n| `captureMessage` | fn | `src/sentry.js:83` | |\n| `addBreadcrumb` | fn | `src/sentry.js:87` | |\n| `ErrorBoundary` | class component | `src/sentry.js:91` | React error boundary reporting to Sentry. |\n| `default` | object | `src/sentry.js:120` | `{init, captureException, captureMessage, addBreadcrumb}` — **omits `ErrorBoundary`**, so named and default surfaces disagree. |\n\nNotes: `@sentry/node` / `@sentry/react` are undeclared optional deps, loaded via `eval(\"require(...)\")` at `src/sentry.js:13` and bare `require` at `:20`. If neither resolves, `Sentry` is `null` (`:29`) and every exported function except `init` throws `TypeError` on call — `captureException` (`:80`), `captureMessage` (`:84`), `addBreadcrumb` (`:88`) have no null guard, unlike `init`.\n\n---\n\n### 1.9 `./otel` → `src/otel.js`\n\n| Export | Kind | Line | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `IS_BOT_KEY` | context key | `src/otel.js:14` | OTel `createContextKey(\"catalyst.is_bot\")`. Internal-ish but needed by anyone propagating bot context. |\n| `withSyncObservability` | fn | `src/otel.js:245` | Wraps a sync fn in a span. |\n| `withObservability` | fn | `src/otel.js:275` | Wraps a sync-or-async fn in a span (always returns a Promise). |\n| `responseFlushMiddleware` | fn | `src/otel.js:328` | Express middleware emitting `response.compress` / `response.flush` spans. **Fragile contract**: must be mounted immediately before `compression()` (documented at `:310-313`). |\n| `default` | object | `src/otel.js:401` | `{init, withObservability, withSyncObservability, responseFlushMiddleware}`. |\n\n**`init` is only available on the default export, never as a named export** — an asymmetry, and the docs use `import ... from \"catalyst-core/otel\"` (`docs/content/02-Guides and Tutorials/06-Observability.md:26`). Also note `IS_BOT_KEY` is named but absent from the default object.\n\nBug worth flagging before a freeze: `src/otel.js:24` compares `process.env.OTEL_ENABLE !== true` — env vars are always strings, so this is `\"true\" !== true` → always `true` → **`init()` always early-returns `{sdk: null, meter: null}`** and OTel never starts. The entire `./otel` entry is effectively inert.\n\nAll 11 `@opentelemetry/*` packages imported at `src/otel.js:1-16` are **undeclared dependencies**.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Deep / undocumented imports by consumers\n\n### 2.1 Specifier census\n\nCounts across `examples/`, `docs/content/`, `docs/src/`, `apps/`, `packages/create-catalyst-app/` (excluding `node_modules/` and `docs/build/`):\n\n| Specifier | Count | In exports map? |\n|---|---|---|\n| `catalyst-core` | 198 | ✅ `.` |\n| `catalyst-core/hooks` | 51 (+3 escaped) | ✅ |\n| `catalyst-core/sentry` | 19 (+6 escaped) | ✅ |\n| `catalyst-core/router/ClientRouter` | 13 | ✅ |\n| `catalyst-core/WebBridge` | 10 (+2 escaped) | ✅ |\n| `catalyst-core/package.json` | 5 | ✅ |\n| **`catalyst-core/universal`** | **4** | ❌ **BROKEN** |\n| `catalyst-core/otel` | 4 (+1 escaped) | ✅ |\n| **`catalyst-core/server/cjsRequire`** | **1** | ❌ **BROKEN** |\n| **`catalyst-core/PluginBridge`** | **1** | ❌ **BROKEN** |\n| `catalyst-core/document` | **0** | ✅ (exported but unused) |\n| `catalyst-core/caching` | **0** | ✅ (exported, unresolvable — §1.3) |\n\n### 2.2 Specifiers NOT in the exports map — must be added or fixed before a freeze\n\n**`catalyst-core/universal`** — does not exist in `src/` at all.\n- `docs/content/02-Guides and Tutorials/01-First Catalyst App/02-Quick-Start.md:365` — `import { Cache } from 'catalyst-core/universal';`\n- `docs/src/js/generated/docs/page-5-02_Guides_and_Tutorials_01_First_Catalyst_App_02_Quick_Start.mjs:444` (generated from the above)\n- Also in `examples/catalyst-companion/build/server/index.js:492` (a built artifact of the docs)\n\nThere is no `src/universal.js`, no `Cache` export anywhere in the package. **The published Quick Start guide contains a copy-pasteable import that throws `ERR_PACKAGE_PATH_NOT_EXPORTED`.** Likely a stale reference to what is now `./caching` (which itself is broken, §1.3). Highest-priority fix.\n\n**`catalyst-core/server/cjsRequire`** — the module exists but is not exported.\n- `src/server/utils/cjsRequire.js:7` — the module's **own JSDoc** advertises `import { cjsRequire } from \"catalyst-core/server/cjsRequire\"`.\n- Note the doc path is `server/cjsRequire` but the file is at `server/utils/cjsRequire.js` — even if added to the map, the documented path is wrong. Either add `\"./server/cjsRequire\": \"./dist/server/utils/cjsRequire.js\"` or correct the JSDoc.\n\n**`catalyst-core/PluginBridge`** — `src/native/plugin-bridge/PluginBridge.js:230` default-exports `pluginNativeBridge`, but there is no `./PluginBridge` export entry. The one reference is a string mention rather than a live import, but it signals intent; if the native plugin story is public, this needs an entry.\n\n### 2.3 `catalyst-core/package.json`\n\nAlready exported (`package.json:20`). Used by `src/vite/vite.config.js:107` and `src/vite/node-loader.mjs:24` to read `_moduleAliases`. Keep.\n\n### 2.4 Consumer-side named-import surface (what a freeze actually must guarantee)\n\nFrom the root `\".\"`, only these names are used anywhere:\n`useCurrentRouteData` (33), `Head` (26), `Body` (26), `Link` (16), `split` (16+4), `Outlet` (15), `RouterProvider` (14), `RouterDataProvider` (14), `hydrationReady` (13), `useParams` (10), `useRouterData` (9), `MetaTag` (8), `useNavigate` (3).\n\nThat's **13 of the ~90 names** the root barrel exposes. The other ~77 are unused by every consumer, doc, example, and template in this repo.\n\n### 2.5 Templates still on the pre-0.3 router\n\n`examples/useai/` imports from `@tata1mg/router`, not `catalyst-core`, despite also importing `catalyst-core/hooks` and `catalyst-core/WebBridge`:\n- `examples/useai/package.json:34` — `\"@tata1mg/router\": \"0.1.0-beta\"`\n- `examples/useai/client/index.js:6` — `import { RouterProvider } from \"@tata1mg/router\"`\n- `examples/useai/src/js/routes/utils.js:2` — `import { RouterDataProvider, MetaTag } from \"@tata1mg/router\"`\n- also `src/js/containers/{App,TicTacToe,AITest,Chess,AIPlayground}/index.js`, `src/js/containers/Home/Home.js:13`, `src/js/pages/Overview/Overview.js:2`\n\nThis directly contradicts `docs/content/03-Routing/03-Router-Data-Provider.md:11` (\"do not install that package in a `0.3.x` application\"). `examples/useai` is a mixed-mode app that shouldn't ship as a 0.3.x reference.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Deprecated / legacy / dead code — removal candidates\n\n### 3.1 Wholly dead files (zero importers anywhere in the repo)\n\n| File | Size | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| **`src/native/bridge/standardizedHooks.js`** | ~700 lines, 3 exports | Zero references outside `audit-report.md`. Exports `useCamera` (`:22`), `useFilePicker` (`:271`), `useIntent` (`:507`) — **name-colliding duplicates** of the live `hooks/` versions. Already flagged in `audit-report.md:67` and `:149`. **Delete.** |\n| **`src/router.js`** | 1 line | `export * from \"@tata1mg/router\"` — the legacy 0.2.x router shim. Not in the exports map, not imported by anything, and `@tata1mg/router` is not a dependency. **Delete.** |\n| **`src/native/bridge/utils/NativeBridge.js`** | ~455 lines | Exports `nativeBridge` default (`:451`) + `NativeBridgeUtil` class (`:454`, comment at `:453` says \"Also export the class for advanced usage\"). No importer. Superseded by `plugin-bridge/PluginBridge.js`. |\n| **`src/native/bridge/utils/CameraUtils.js`** | ~214 lines | `export default CameraUtils` (`:214`). No importer. |\n| **`src/native/bridge/errors.js`** | ~290 lines | 6 exports (`ERROR_CATEGORIES:7`, `ERROR_CODES:18`, `ERROR_DEFINITIONS:52`, `createStandardError:166`, `translateError:186`, `isDevelopment:286`). No importer. |\n| **`src/native/bridge/safeArea.js`** | 4 exports | `DEFAULT_INSETS:1`, `getSafeAreaFromGlobal:22`, `setSafeAreaGlobal:35`, `getSafeArea:43`. No importer — `hooks/useSafeArea.js` doesn't use it. |\n| **`src/web-router/context.jsx`** | `OneMgRouterContext:12` | Live (used by `MetaTag.jsx:3` and `RouterDataProvider.jsx:11`) but **not** exported publicly — listed here only because the stale `src/web-router/types/context.d.ts:9` declares it as public API. |\n\n### 3.2 Dead code within live files\n\n| Location | Issue |\n|---|---|\n| `src/web-router/hooks.jsx:12-68` | 57 lines of commented-out `navigationDirection` + real `useNavigateWithTransition` implementation. The live version (`:70-72`) is a no-op `return useNavigate()`. The helper `wait()` (`: