e code so this can't rot again.**\n\n## 4. The app contract\n\nThe framework imports five files from every app by fixed path (`server/document.js`, `server/index.js`, `src/js/containers/App`, `src/js/routes/utils`, `src/js/store`) and requires six aliases in the app's package.json. create-catalyst-app scaffolds all of it, so it's already our contract in practice — it's just undocumented and slightly buggy.\n\n- a) Keep the design; before rc.1: fix the alias-precedence bug (client build and SSR currently resolve differently when an app redefines an alias), document the five files + six aliases in the API reference, and make the startup validator fail with a clear error instead of logging and continuing.\n- b) Redesign it now: the app passes routes/App/store/document into a bootstrap call instead of the framework importing by path. Cleaner, but a breaking rework of core, all six templates, and the docs right before an RC.\n\n**Recommendation: (a). The redesign is good 1.x/2.0 work alongside the runtime adapter, not pre-RC work.**\n\n## 5. Which in-flight feature PRs make 1.0\n\nEach of these adds public API. Landed before rc.1 it freezes immediately with no bake time; otherwise it ships in a 1.x minor: #328 (custom API routes), #254 (web-fallback hooks), #249 (biometric login), #239 (`useVideoStream`), #261 (parallel fetches + router caching).\n\n**Recommendation: default everything to 1.1; land before the RC only what's already production-validated. New API in minors is cheap — un-freezing API is not.**\n\n## 6. Caching — 1.0 feature or not?\n\n`./caching` re-exports `@tata1mg/api-caching`, which is neither declared nor installed — importing it throws today — and the Quick Start teaches `catalyst-core/universal`, which doesn't exist. Either caching becomes a real, declared, frozen 1.0 feature, or the entry goes away and comes back in 1.x. The docs get fixed either way.\n\n**Recommendation: drop the entry for 1.0. It's broken today and nobody's using it, so it clearly